1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,216
A native Rust IDE for embedded development, in your terminal.

2
00:00:04,416 --> 00:00:07,344
Build with GCC, and the error is one keypress away.

3
00:00:09,880 --> 00:00:11,215
Fix it, and build again.

4
00:00:13,042 --> 00:00:15,127
Then hand a task to an AI agent.

5
00:00:15,177 --> 00:00:18,809
EmbedIDE drives the Claude Code or Codex CLI you already use.

6
00:00:20,009 --> 00:00:23,485
It edits files, builds, and runs your program, and every step is visible.

7
00:00:28,279 --> 00:00:30,016
Review every change, or revert it.

8
00:00:31,516 --> 00:00:33,603
EmbedIDE is open source and in alpha.

9
00:00:33,653 --> 00:00:35,501
Try it, and tell us what breaks.
